 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? How many miles you put on it in a season? It's usually a couple of times a year, after the first few months and then every few hundred miles. The sidewall should just give gently, not any resistance. If it feels hard at the valve, add bit more air. That's fine, most people do. Just pump up after each ride for now. No, go indoors. Rain doesn't affect the pressure much, but standing something wet on the rim does, so keep it off. And check the tyre for cracks if it' been wet.",
